1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://ee.domaindlx.com/paulsengeneology/ancestry/pafn10.htm#680 dead link
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Iver Hansen Wolf'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Iver Hanssen Wolf ( Wulff ) was born in Nakskov, Denmark, 1628. He was married in Nakskov or in Haderselv around 1660. He died in 1690 while living in Ervik in Trondenes, Norway. Iver Wolff was the son of fogd and customs cashier 
2 CONC Hans Wolff in Nakskov. Iver Wolff was appointed fogd over Senjen by king Fredrik III shortly after 1660. After some strife with the widow of the last fogd, Mathias T. Holst, he moved to Ervik in Norway which had been the fogds off
2 CONC icial residence as far back as man could remember. This happened arround 1662-63. In 1666, Wolff became the ombudsman for Joakim Irgens when he took over the crowns goods in the Nordlands, the so called Irgin's goods, while he con
2 CONC tinued to be the king's fogd in Senjen. Then it was discovered that inconsistencies existed in the accounts, and in 1669 he was suspended as fogd, but "stillet til Kongens nåde" (put under the King's mercy). After five years, he g
2 CONC ot his job as fogd back. This happened on 10 July 1674. Irgens was now dead. Wolff "forpakted" the income of the Irvin goods for 4 years to the widow Cornelia Bichers. That will say, he paid her a sum certain and he in turn would 
2 CONC keep the income from the operation of the farms and businesses. On this agreement, however, he lost circa 100 rdlr per year because of fishing that failed and poor corn crops attributed to frost and cold weather. Iver Hansen died,
2 CONC  while still a fogd, in 1690, as a poor man. When the estate was probated there was a deficit of 285 rdlr that his two sons in law were held responsible for. Father: Hans Jacobsen WOLF Mother: Karen MATHIASDATTER RESIDENCE: 10 Jul
2 CONC  1674, Ble Fogd i Senja OCCUPATION: Fogd i Senja Family 1 : Maren Paulsdatter HADERSLEV
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Fogd , (Skatteinnkrever) i Kvæfjord.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Kvæfjordboka bind 2, nr. 1 Strand. Redaktør JAC. NORMAN:  Om "Wulfene på Strand" vises til ingeniør Nils Vigs bok, der han referer til til slektsforskern Alfred Tangens opptegnelser. Disse går ut på at Iver Hansen Wolf f. ca  1628
2 CONC  i Naskov, Danmark, d. 1690 som foged i Ervik, kom med Wulfnamnet til Norge.  Se interessant slektstavle Vebostad nr.  1. Hans sønn: Povel Iversen Wolf f. ca. 1666, var i 1704 kontorist hos fogden Bremer i Ervik, som var g. m.  El
2 CONC se Marie Iversd. Wolff, tante til Iver Povelson Wulf og søster til Povel Iversen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Han ble utnevnt til fogd over Senjens fogderi den 10. juli 1674.  https://godfjord.no/kvafjordboka-2-6      Se også under Vebostad.      https://godfjord.no/kvafjordboka-2-4
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://ee.domaindlx.com/paulsengeneology/ancestry/pafn10.htm#680 dead link
2 CONT
2 CONT Iver Hansen Wolff
2 CONT
2 CONT Iver Hanssen Wolff ( Wulff ) was born in Nakskov, Denmark, 1628. He was married in Nakskov or in Haderselv around 1660. He died in 1690 while living in Ervik in Trondenes. Iver Wolff was the son of fogd and customs cashier Hans Wo
2 CONC lff in Nakskov. Iver Wolff was appointed fogd over Senjen by king Fredrik III shortly after 1660. After some strife with the widow of the last fogd, Mathias T. Holst, he moved to Ervik which had been the fogds official residence a
2 CONC s far back as man could remember. This happened arround 1662-63. In 1666, Wolff became the ombudsman for Joakim Irgens when he took over the crowns goods in the Nordlands, the so called Irgin's goods, while he continued to be the 
2 CONC king's fogd in Senjen. Then it was discovered that inconsistencies existed in the accounts, and in 1669 he was suspended as fogd, but "stillet til Kongens nåde" (put under the King's mercy). After five years, he got his job as fog
2 CONC d back. This happened on 10 July 1674. Irgens was now dead. Wolff "forpakted" the income of the Irvin goods for 4 years to the widow Cornelia Bichers. That will say, he paid her a sum certain and he in turn would keep the income f
2 CONC rom the operation of the farms and businesses. On this agreement, however, he lost circa 100 rdlr per year because of fishing that failed and poor corn crops attributed to frost and cold weather. Iver Hansen died, while still a fo
2 CONC gd, in 1690, as a poor man. When the estate was probated there was a deficit of 285 rdlr that his two sons in law were held responsible for. Father: Hans Jacobsen WOLF Mother: Karen MATHIASDATTER RESIDENCE: 10 Jul 1674, Ble Fogd i
2 CONC  Senja OCCUPATION: Fogd i Senja Family 1 : Maren Paulsdatter HADERSLEV
2 CONT
2 CONT Fogd , (Skatteinnkrever) i Kvæfjord.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kvæfjordboka bind 2, nr. 1 Strand. Redaktør JAC. NORMAN: Om "Wulfene på Strand" vises til ingeniør Nils Vigs bok, der han referer til til slektsforskern Alfred Tangens opptegnelser. Disse går ut på at Iver Hansen Wolf f. ca 1628 i
2 CONC  Naskov, Danmark, d. 1690 som foged i Ervik, kom med Wulfnamnet til Norge. Se interessant slektstavle Vebostad nr. 1. Hans sønn: Povel Iversen Wolf f. ca. 1666, var i 1704 kontorist hos fogden Bremer i Ervik, som var g. m. Else Ma
2 CONC rie Iversd. Wolff, tante til Iver Povelson Wulf og søster til Povel Iversen. Han ble utnevnt til fogd over Senjens fogderi den 10. juli 1674.
